pact assessment.	[]	https://mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	verified	Binding Precedent	IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT (PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI)\nAT CHENNAI\n\nCASE NO: W.P. No. 18920 of 2026\nCNR NUMBER: MHC010214892026\nDECISION DATE: 2026-03-02\nYEAR: 2026\n\nCORAM / BENCH:\nHon'ble Justice D. Krishnakumar & Justice P.B. Balaji\n\nPARTIES:\nK. Balasubramanian and 14 others\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nState of Tamil Nadu represented by Principal Secretary, Revenue Department & District Collector, Kancheepuram\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nRight to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition Act 2013, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nRFCTLARR Act Section 11, RFCTLARR Act Section 15, Article 226, Article 300A\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nLand Acquisition, Social Impact Assessment, Public Purpose, Natural Justice, Writ of Mandamus\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nPetitioners' agricultural lands were acquired for airport expressway expansion without publishing mandatory Social Impact Assessment study report under Section 4 and without hearing objections under Section 15.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether compliance with Social Impact Assessment under Chapter II of RFCTLARR Act 2013 is mandatory prior to preliminary notification?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nSection 4 of the 2013 Act imposes an inescapable statutory obligation on the government to prepare and evaluate SIA in consultation with local authorities.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nAcquisition proceedings initiated without prior Social Impact Assessment study under RFCTLARR Act 2013 suffer from fatal jurisdictional defect and are void ab initio.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; Acquisition notifications under Act 30 of 2013 quashed for failure to conduct social impact assessment.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice D. Krishnakumar & Justice P.B. Balaji\nMadras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t
