stantive equality. It was unequivocally established as binding law that statutory prerequisites and constitutional safeguards cannot be circumvented, and non-compliance invalidates the impugned proceedings.	["Prima facie establishment of statutory cause of action within limitation period", "Discharge of statutory burden of proof to required legal standard", "Strict adherence to procedural fairness and natural justice safeguards", "Compliance with mandatory statutory prerequisites prior to initiation of proceedings"]	Decided	["Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India (1978) 1 SCC 248", "State of Haryana v. Bhajan Lal 1992 Supp (1) SCC 335", "Lalita Kumari v. Govt of U.P. (2014) 2 SCC 1"]	\N	unverified	Precedential status not checked	\N	1	f
