ull maternity benefits on equal footing with regular staff, in accordance with social justice under Article 42. It was unequivocally established as binding law that statutory prerequisites and constitutional safeguards cannot be circumvented, and non-compliance invalidates the impugned proceedings.	["Legality: State action authorized by valid and competent law", "Legitimate Aim: Measure serves a pressing and justifiable constitutional purpose", "Proportionality: Rational nexus between means adopted and objective sought with least intrusive impact", "Procedural Due Process: Adherence to principles of natural justice and non-arbitrariness"]	Decided	["K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India (2017) 10 SCC 1", "Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India (1978) 1 SCC 248", "Navtej Singh Johar v. Union of India (2018) 10 SCC 1"]	\N	unverified	Precedential status not checked	\N	1	f
