nSantosh Kerba Wharge ….Petitioner\n-------\nMr. Nitin K. Jadhav i/b. Mr. Rajiv A. Jadhav for the Petitioner.\n-------\nCORAM : GAUTAM A. ANKHAD, J.\nDATE : 22nd OCTOBER, 2026.\nP.C. :\n1. This Petition is filed seeking Legal Heirship Certificate under\nSection 2 of Bombay Regulation (VIII) of 1827 in respect of the\nDeceased – Kerba Gundappa Wharge also known as Keraba Gundappa\nVharage who at the time of his death was residing at Post : Kaneri,\nTaluka : Panhala, District : Kolhapur – 416 230. The Deceased died\nintestate on 21st October, 2017 and a copy of the death certificate is\nannexed at Exhibit ‘A’ to the Petition.\n2. The Petitioner is the only son and the only legal heir of the\nDeceased. It is further stated that the parents and wife of the Deceased\n1/3\n12-MPT-1191-2026.doc Gauri Gaekwad\n\nhave predeceased the Deceased and there are no other heirs and next-of-\nkin of the Deceased. It is in this background that the Petitioner seeks the\nHeirship Certificate.\n3. The reasons for filing this Petition are stated at paragraph no.6 of\nthe Petition. It is also stated that the Petitioner has not filed any other\nPetition for Heirship Certificate, Succession Certificate, Probate or\nLetters of Administration and there is no impediment to the grant of the\nreliefs in this Petition.\n4. As far as the delay is concerned, the same is condoned in the light\nof the judgment of this Court in Ganpati Vinayak Achwal 1 wherein this\nCourt has held that the right to apply is a continuous right which is\ncapable of being exercised at any time after the death of the Deceased,\nas long as the right to do so exists.\n5. In view of the statements/undertakings contained in the Petition,\nwhich are accepted, Miscellaneous Petition No.1191 of 2026 is allowed\nin terms of prayer clause (a), which reads as under :\n(a) This Honble Court be pleased to declare that Shri\nSantosh Kerba Wharge, the Son of the deceased, is\n1 2014 SCC OnLine Bom 1193\n2/3\n12-MPT-1191-2026.doc Gauri Gaekwad\n\nthe only heir and legal representative of Late Kerba\nGundappa Wharge also known as Keraba\nGundappa Vharage, under the provisions of\nBombay regulation VIII of 1827.\n6. Issue of Proclamation is dispensed with.\n7. The Department is directed to issue the Legal Heirship Certificate\nwithin a period of six weeks from today.\n[ GAUTAM A. ANKHAD, J. ]\n3/3\n12-MPT-1191-2026.doc Gauri Gaekwad	3	t
