ed seeking Legal Heirship Certificate under\nSection 2 of Bombay Regulation (VIII) of 1827 in respect of the\nDeceased – Nalini Bapu Bhalerao alias Nalini Bapurao Bhalerao who at\nthe time of her death was residing at K-6, 115, Swatimitra Co-operative\nHousing Society Limited, 7 Gulmohar Cross Road, JVPD Scheme,\nAndheri (East), Mumbai - 400 049. The Deceased died intestate on\n10th June, 2021 and a copy of the death certificate is annexed at Exhibit\n‘A’ to the Petition.\n1/4\n7-MPT-1186-2026.doc Gauri Gaekwad\n\n2. Petitioner No.1 is the unmarried sister and Petitioner Nos.2 and 3\nare the nephews of the Deceased. At paragraph no.4, the Petitioners have\nfurnished details of the only surviving legal heirs and next-of-kin of the\nDeceased as follows :\nSr. Name and address of the legal heirs of Age Relation with the\nNo. the deceased deceased\n1. Sunanda Bapurao Bhalerao 81 yrs. Unmarried Sister\nresiding at K-6/115, Swatimitra CHSL,\nA-Wing, Gulmohar Cross Road No.7,\nNear Ecole Mondiale, JVPD Scheme,\nJuhu, Andheri (East), Mumbai – 400\n049, Maharashtra.\n(herein Petitioner No.1)\n2. Shreyas Chandrakant Bhalerao 48 yrs. Nephew\nresiding at K-6/115, Swatimitra CHSL, (Son of\nA-Wing, Gulmohar Cross Road No.7, Deceased\nNear Ecole Mondiale, JVPD Scheme, Brother of\nJuhu, Andheri (East), Mumbai – 400 Deceased)\n049, Maharashtra.\n(herein Petitioner No.2)\n3. Bhushan Chandrakant Bhalerao 44 yrs. Nephew\nresiding at Row House No.F/3, Opp. (Son of\nSawant Garage, Bijlinagar, Deceased\nChinchwadgaon, Pune - 411 033, Brother of\nMaharashtra. Deceased)\n(herein Petitioner No.3)\n3. It is further stated that the parents of the Deceased have\npredeceased the Deceased and there are no other heirs and next-of-kin of\n2/4\n7-MPT-1186-2026.doc Gauri Gaekwad\n\nthe Deceased. It is in this background that the Petitioners seek the\nHeirship Certificate.\n4. The reasons for filing this Petition are stated at paragraph no.6 of\nthe Petition. It is also stated that the Petitioners or the legal heirs have\nnot filed any other Petition for Heirship Certificate, Succession\nCertificate, Probate or Letters of Administration and there is no\nimpediment to the grant of the reliefs in this Petition.\n5. As far as the delay is concerned, the same is condoned in the light\nof the judgment of this Court in Ganpati Vinayak Achwal 1 wherein this\nCourt has held that the right to apply is a continuous right which is\ncapable of being exercised at any time after the death of the Deceased,\nas long as the right to do so exists.\n6. In view of the statements/undertakings contained in the Petition,\nwhich are accepted, Miscellaneous Petition No.1186 of 2026 is allowed\nin terms of prayer clause (a), which reads as under :\n(a) This Hon’ble Court be pleased to issue a Legal\nHeirship Certificate to the petitioners under the\n1 2014 SCC OnLine Bom 1193\n3/4\n7-MPT-1186-2026.doc Gauri Gaekwad\n\nprovision of Bombay Regulation VII of 1827\ncertifying that follows persons i.e. (1) Sunanda\nBapurao Bhalerao (Sister) (2) Shreyas Chandrakant\nBhalerao (Nephew) and (3) Bhushan Chandrakant\nBhalerao (Nephew) are only Legal Heirs of the\ndeceased abovenamed i.e. Nalini Bapu Bhalerao\nalias Nalini Bapurao Bhalerao.\n7. Issue of Proclamation is dispensed with.\n8. The Department is directed to issue the Legal Heirship Certificate\nwithin a period of six weeks from today.\n[ GAUTAM A. ANKHAD, J. ]\n4/4\n7-MPT-1186-2026.doc Gauri Gaekwad	4	t
