ter of the instant writ petition is\nthe notice dated 17.09.2026 whereby and\nwhereunder the prescribed Authority has fixed the\ndate of meeting on motion for removal of Pradhan\non 29.09.2026.\n3. At the time of hearing, it is submitted at the bar\nthat pursuant to the said notice of motion, the\nremoval of Pradhan has been effected.\n4. The learned Advocate appearing on behalf of the\nwrit petitioner submits before this Court that\nsimilar such notice was issued on 05.10.2026\n\n2\nwhere the proposed meeting was scheduled to be\nheld on 13.10.2026, the date of which has already\nbeen expired.\n5. In view of such, this Court finds that with the\npassage of time, the instant writ petition has\nbecome infructuous and nothing remains to be\ndecided in respect of the impugned notice.\n6. With the aforesaid observation, the instant writ\npetition is disposed of.\n(Partha Sarathi Sen, J.)	2	t
