. adv.,\nMr. Ratul Biswas,\nMr. Kaushik Chowdhury.\n…. For the WBBPE\n1. Affidavit-of-service filed on behalf of the writ\npei6ttoner, in Court today, is taken on record.\n2. The writ petitioner, respondent State and the\nWest Bengal Board of Primary Education are\nrepresented by their respective learned counsel.\n3. At the time of hearing, Mr. Chowdhury, learned\nadvocate appearing on behalf of the writ\npetitioner submits before this Court that the writ\npetitioner is aggrieved for non-consideration of\nhis representation dated 16.03.2026 as has been\nannexed at page 26 of the instant writ petition,\nby the respondent no. 2 authority.\n\n2\n4. Mr. Kaushik Chowdhury, learned advocate\nappearing on behalf of the respondent no.\n2/Board submits before this Court that the\nsubject matter of the said representation dated\n16.03.2026 is the policy decision of the State\nand therefore, the respondent Board is not the\ncompetent authority to take a conscious decision\nof the matter.\n5. Learned advocate for the respondent State\nsubmits before this Court that the instant writ\npetition is devoid of merit.\n6. On careful perusal of the entire materials as\nplaced before this Court, it appears that the writ\npetitioner submitted its representation dated\n16.03.2026 with the respondent no. 2 authority\nwith a request to change the medium of\nimparting education from Bengali to Hindi in\nrespect of 50 seats out of 100 seats.\n7. No cogent reason has been shown by the\nrespondent no. 2/Board as to what prompted\nthem to go for eternal slumber over such\nrepresentation.\n8. In view of such, this Court while disposing the\ninstant writ petition directs the respondent no. 2\nauthority to consider the representation dated\n16.03.2026 in accordance with law and after\ngiving an opportunity of hearing to the writ\npetitioner and/or his authorized representative,\n\n3\nshall pass a reasoned order and shall forthwith\ncommunicate the same to the writ petitioner,\npreferably by e-mail, if the e-mail details of the\nwrit petitioner is provided to him at the time of\nhearing.\n9. The entire exercise, as indicated in the foregoing\nparagraph, is to be completed by the respondent\nno. 2 authority positively within 45 working days\nfrom the date of communication of the server\ncopy of this order.\n10. The time limit as fixed by this Court is\nperemptory and mandatory.\n11. Liberty is given to the learned advocate on\nrecord of the writ petitioner to communicate the\nserver copy of this order to the respondent no. 2\nauthority, who is directed to act on the server\ncopy of this order.\n12. With the aforementioned observation, the\ninstant writ petition is disposed of.\n13. Before parting with, it is, however made clear\nthat while disposing of the instant writ petition\nthis Court has not gone into the merits of the\nrepresentation dated 16.03.2026, as submitted\nby the writ petitioner and thus, all points are\nkept open for adjudication by the respondent no.\n2 authority.\n(Partha Sarathi Sen, J.)	3	t
