://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District.\n(Crime No.589/2026)\n3. M.Ashok\n4.C.Kanagaraj\n5.R.Boopathi Kannan\n6.Manoj\n7.M.Mayakannan\n8.P.Priyadharshini\n9.M.Chandra\n10.Sind	[]	Principles governing criminal jurisdiction and interim protections.	[]	Petition disposed of in terms of statutory safeguards.	[]	\N	unverified	Precedential status not checked	CRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nBEFORE THE MADURAI BENCH OF MADRAS HIGH COURT\nDATED: 16-10-2026\nCORAM\nTHE HON'BLE MR.JUSTICE S.KARTHIKEYAN\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nCNR:{HCMD011431722026}\n1. M.Selvakumar\nS/o. Mookan,\nKomanapatti, Sathampaadi,\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District- 624 401\n2. C.Prabakaran\nS/o. Chellam,\nKomanapatti, Sathampaadi,\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District - 624 401.\n3. S.Gokul\nS/o. Subiramani,\nKomanapatti, Sathampaadi,\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District - 624 401.\n4. R.Ajay\nS/o. Ravi,\nKomanapatti, Sathampaadi,\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District- 624 401.\n..Appellant(s)\nVs\n1. The State ofTamilnadu rep by\nThe Deputy superintendent of Police,\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District.\n2. State Of Tamilnadu Rep By Inspector Of Police,\nNatham\nPolice station,\n__________\nPage 1 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District.\n(Crime No.589/2026)\n3. M.Ashok\n4.C.Kanagaraj\n5.R.Boopathi Kannan\n6.Manoj\n7.M.Mayakannan\n8.P.Priyadharshini\n9.M.Chandra\n10.Sindhuja Shri (Minor),\nRepresented by her father B.Siva\n11.A.Parimala\n..Respondent(s)\n(R 4 to R 11 were impleaded vide order dated 16.10.2026)\nPRAYER: Criminal Appeal filed under Section 14 A(2) of the SC/ST\n(POA) Amendment Act, 2015 to set aside the order passed in\nCrl.M.P.No.268 of 2026 dated 30.09.2026 on the file of the Special Court\nfor Exclusive Trial of Cases under SC/ST (POA) Act, Dindigul and\nenlarge the appellants 1 to 4/Accused Nos.3, 7, 9 and 10 on bail in\nconnection with Crime No.589 of 2026 on the file of the respondent\npolice.\nFor Appellant(s): Mr.S.Arunnithy\nFor Respondent(s): Mr.G.Ganesh Kumar (R1 & R2)\nGovernment Advocate\n(Criminal Side)\n__________\nPage 2 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nMr.K.Pandiarajan\nFor victims\nJUDGMENT\nThis appeal is directed against the order declining to grant bail to\nthe appellants by the learned Special Court for Exclusive Trial of Cases\nunder the SC/ST (POA) Act, Dindigul, in Crime No.589 of 2026.\\\n2.The learned counsel for the appellants submitted that, when the\nVinayakar idol was taken in procession in connection with the Vinayakar\nChathurthi festival, a quarrel erupted between two groups of people\nbelonging to Komanapatti, Natham Taluk. In this connection, the present\ncase was registered in Crime No.589 of 2026 for the offences punishable\nunder Sections 191(2), 191(3), 296(b), 115(2), 118(1), 351(3) and 79 of\nthe Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), and Sections 3(1)(r), 3(1)(s), 3(1)\n(2a)(C), 3(1)(y), 3(1)(w)(i), 3(1)(2)(ii) and 3(2)(va) of the SC/ST (POA)\nAct. A counter-case was registered in Crime No.590 of 2026 against 22\naccused for the offences punishable under Sections 296, 296(b), 191(2),\n191(3), 119(2), 118(1), 351(2) and 79 of the BNS and Section 92(b) of\nthe Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016.\n3.The learned counsel further submitted that, in the counter-case,\n__________\nPage 3 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\n22 persons were arrayed as accused, of whom four were arrested and the\nothers obtained anticipatory bail. The arrested persons were also\nsubsequently released on bail. Therefore, the learned counsel prayed that\nthe appellants be enlarged on bail.\n4.The learned Government Advocate (Criminal Side) submitted\nthat, based on the complaint lodged by the third respondent, the present\ncase came to be registered by the respondent police. There was a clash\nbetween two groups belonging to different communities in connection\nwith the procession of the Ganesha idol during the Vinayakar Chathurthi\nfestival. In this connection, a case and a counter-case were registered. In\nthe counter-case, 22 persons were arrayed as accused, and all of them\nwere granted bail or anticipatory bail, as the case may be. In the present\ncase, 14 persons were arrayed as accused. Of them, ten persons\nsurrendered pursuant to the order passed by this Court in Crl.O.P.(MD)\nNo.22719 of 2026 and obtained bail from the trial Court. Therefore, the\nlearned Government Advocate strongly opposed the grant of bail to the\nappellants.\n5.Notice was issued to the victims, who appeared in person before\nthis Court today.\n__________\nPage 4 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\n6.The victims are represented by their learned counsel. The\nlearned counsel for the victims submitted that, during the Vinayakar\nChathurthi festival, when they took the Ganesha idol in procession, the\naccused unlawfully assembled, attacked them with deadly weapons and\nabused them in filthy language by referring to their caste names. The\nlearned counsel further submitted that, if the accused are released on bail,\nthey may issue further threats to the victims. Therefore, the learned\ncounsel strongly opposed the grant of bail to the appellants.\n7.This Court has given its thoughtful consideration to the rival\nsubmissions made by the learned counsel appearing on either side.\n8.It is the case of the prosecution that, on 18.09.2026, at around\n8.30 a.m., a procession of the Ganesha idol was taken out in Komanapatti\nVillage in connection with the Vinayakar Chathurthi festival. At that\ntime, a clash broke out between two groups of people belonging to the\nsaid village, resulting in injuries to persons on both sides. In this\nconnection, Crime No.589 of 2026 was registered against the appellants,\nwhile Crime No.590 of 2026 was registered against the members of the\nother group.\n__________\nPage 5 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\n9.In the counter-case, all the accused were granted bail or\nanticipatory bail, as the case may be. In the present case also, except for\nthe appellants, all the other accused surrendered pursuant to the order\npassed by this Court in Crl.O.P.(MD) No.22719 of 2026 and obtained\nbail from the trial Court. It is further seen that the injured persons have\nalready been discharged from the hospital and are physically present\nbefore this Court.\n10.Considering all the above circumstances, this Court is inclined\nto allow this criminal appeal, subject to the imposition of stringent\nconditions.\n11.Accordingly, this Criminal Appeal is allowed, and the order\npassed by the learned Special Court for Exclusive Trial of Cases under\nthe SC/ST (POA) Act, Dindigul, in Crl.M.P.No.268 of 2026, dated\n30.09.2026, is hereby set aside. The appellants are ordered to be released\non bail, subject to the following conditions:\ni. The appellants shall execute a bond for a sum of Rs.20,000/-\n(Rupees Twenty Thousand only) each, with two sureties each for a like\nsum, to the satisfaction of the learned Special Court for Exclusive Trial of\n__________\nPage 6 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nCases under the SC/ST (POA) Act, Dindigul.\nii. The appellants and their sureties shall submit copies of their\nAadhaar cards or any other identity cards issued by the Government as\nproof of their residential addresses.\niii. The appellants shall file affidavits of undertaking before the\nrespondent police, undertaking that they will not involve themselves in\nany criminal activity in the future.\niv. The appellants shall reside in Trichy and shall not enter the\nvillage or contact the victims or the de facto complainant, either directly\nor through electronic means, during the period of bail.\nv. The appellants shall not contact the victims or their family\nmembers, either directly or indirectly, with a view to influencing them to\nwithdraw the complaint.\nvi. The appellants shall reside in Trichy and report before the\nInspector of Police, Malaikottai Police Station, Trichy, daily at 10.30\na.m., until further orders, except on days when their appearance is\n__________\nPage 7 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nrequired before the trial Court.\nvii. In the event of any violation of the above conditions by the\nappellants, the respondent police shall be at liberty to move an\napplication seeking cancellation of bail.\n16-10-2026\n(1/2)\nIndex: Yes/No\nSpeaking/Non-speaking order\nNeutral Citation: Yes/No\nPS\n__________\nPage 8 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nTo\n1.The Special Court for Exclusive Trial of Cases under SC/ST (POA)\nAct, Dindigul.\n2.The Deputy superintendent of Police,\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District.\n3.The Inspector Of Police,\nNatham Police station,\nNatham Taluk,\nDindigul District.\n4.The District Jail,\nDindigul.\n5.The Additional Public Prosecutor,\nMadurai Bench of Madras High Court,\nMadurai.\n__________\nPage 9 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\nS.KARTHIKEYAN, J.\nPS\nCRL A(MD) No. 1224 of 2026\n(1/2)\n16-10-2026\n__________\nPage 10 of 10\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis	10	t
