?"]	The Court held that: Historical ruling on unstamped arbitration clauses which held such agreements unenforceable, subsequently overruled by the unanimous 7-judge curative bench in December 2023. It was unequivocally established as binding law that statutory prerequisites and constitutional safeguards cannot be circumvented, and non-compliance invalidates the impugned proceedings.	["Existence of prima facie valid arbitration agreement in writing", "Arbitrability of subject matter under commercial jurisdiction", "Minimal judicial interference principle under Section 5 strictly adhered to", "Compliance with limitation period for filing Section 34 petition within 90 days (plus 30 days condonable)"]	Decided	["Associate Builders v. Delhi Development Authority (2015) 3 SCC 49", "Vidya Drolia v. Durga Trading Corp (2021) 2 SCC 1", "Perkins Eastman Architects DPC v. HSCC (India) Ltd (2020) 20 SCC 760"]	\N	unverified	Precedential status not checked	\N	1	f
