ust be 'just, fair, and reasonable', linking Articles 14, 19, and 21 as the interlocked Golden Triangle. It was unequivocally established as binding law that statutory prerequisites and constitutional safeguards cannot be circumvented, and non-compliance invalidates the impugned proceedings.	["Proximity of speech to public disorder or state security under Article 19(2)", "Absence of overbreadth, chilling effect, or unconstitutional vagueness in statutory terms", "Intermediary safe harbor immunity conditioned on actual court order or government takedown request", "Adherence to procedural safeguards and review committee oversight for digital blocking"]	Decided	["Shreya Singhal v. Union of India (2015) 5 SCC 1", "K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India (2017) 10 SCC 1", "Anuradha Bhasin v. Union of India (2020) 3 SCC 637"]	\N	unverified	Precedential status not checked	\N	1	f
