n'ble Justice R. Subramanian\n\nPARTIES:\nUnited India Insurance Company Limited\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nLakshmi and 3 others (Legal heirs of deceased Rajan)\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nMotor Vehicles Act 1988\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nMotor Vehicles Act Section 166, Motor Vehicles Act Section 173\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nMotor Accident Claims, Multiplier Method, Future Prospects, Loss of Dependency, Pranay Sethi\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nTribunal awarded Rs. 42 Lakhs compensation adding 50% future prospects for a 46-year-old self-employed mason. Insurance company appealed on excessive quantum.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. What is the appropriate addition for future prospects for a self-employed deceased aged between 40 and 50 years under National Insurance Co. Ltd. v. Pranay Sethi?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nConstitution Bench in Pranay Sethi settled that where deceased was self-employed and aged 40-50, addition for future prospects must be 25%, not 50%.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nFor self-employed victims aged between 40 and 50 years in motor accident claims, future prospects addition is legally capped at 25%.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nCivil Miscellaneous Appeal Partly Allowed; Compensation recomputed from Rs. 42 Lakhs to Rs. 34.5 Lakhs following Pranay Sethi multiplier.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice R. Subramanian\nMadras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t
