ON DATE: 2026-03-10\nYEAR: 2026\n\nCORAM / BENCH:\nHon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi\n\nPARTIES:\nM. Karuppasamy\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nThe State represented by Sub-Inspector of Police, Oomachikulam Police Station, Madurai District\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nCode of Criminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita 2023\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nCrPC Section 438, BNSS Section 482, BNS Section 115, BNS Section 352\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nAnticipatory Bail, Pre-Arrest Bail, Civil Dispute, Custodial Interrogation, Cooperation\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nPetitioner sought anticipatory bail in an FIR alleging boundary dispute altercation. No grievous injury was suffered by the complainant and weapon was already recovered.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether custodial interrogation is indispensable in land boundary scuffle when weapon is recovered?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nApplying Arnesh Kumar and Satender Kumar Antil principles on personal liberty under Article 21 and Section 438 CrPC / 482 BNSS.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nWhere offense carries punishment under 7 years and custodial interrogation is unnecessary, anticipatory bail should normally be granted.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nAnticipatory Bail Granted with conditions; Petitioner directed to appear before IO daily for 2 weeks.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t
