 DATE: 2026-03-22\nYEAR: 2026\n\nCORAM / BENCH:\nHon'ble Justice G. Ilangovan\n\nPARTIES:\nA. John Kennedy\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nIntelligence Officer, Narcotics Control Bureau (NCB), Madurai Sub Zone\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nNarcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act 1985\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nNDPS Act Section 8(c), NDPS Act Section 20(b)(ii)(C), NDPS Act Section 37\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nNDPS Bail, Commercial Quantity, Section 37 NDPS, Twin Conditions, Reasonable Grounds\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nPetitioner was apprehended with 42 kg of Ganja (commercial quantity). Petitioner moved second regular bail application alleging procedural non-compliance with Section 50 NDPS Act.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether non-compliance with Section 50 can be decided at bail stage when search was of vehicle and luggage?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nSection 37 NDPS mandates satisfaction that accused is not guilty and unlikely to commit offense while on bail.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nSection 50 NDPS Act applies only to personal search of the accused, not vehicle search. Twin conditions under Section 37 bar bail in commercial quantity seizure.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nBail Application Dismissed; Commercial quantity recovery bars bail under Section 37 of NDPS Act.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice G. Ilangovan\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t
