026\nCNR NUMBER: HCMD010567892026\nDECISION DATE: 2026-01-15\nYEAR: 2026\n\nCORAM / BENCH:\nHon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar\n\nPARTIES:\nSubramanian and Another (Defendants 1 & 2)\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nPitchaiammal and 4 others (Plaintiffs)\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nCode of Civil Procedure 1908, Limitation Act 1963\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nCPC Order VII Rule 11(d), Limitation Act Article 58, CPC Section 115\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nRejection of Plaint, Order VII Rule 11, Barred by Limitation, Clever Drafting, Civil Revision\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nSuit for declaration of title filed 18 years after registered partition deed. Defendants filed application under Order VII Rule 11(d) CPC to reject plaint as barred by limitation.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Whether meaningful reading of plaint demonstrates suit is barred by limitation despite clever drafting?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nApplying Dahiben v. Arvindbhai Kalyanji Bhanusali: Plaint must be rejected if averments show claim is barred by limitation without trial.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nWhere averments in plaint read as a whole disclose that right to sue accrued beyond 3 years under Article 58 Limitation Act, plaint is liable to rejection under Order VII Rule 11(d) CPC.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nCivil Revision Petition Allowed; Order of Trial Court set aside; Plaint rejected under Order VII Rule 11(d) CPC as barred by limitation.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t
