.R. Swaminathan\n\nPARTIES:\nT. Packiaraj (Temple Worshipper)\n... Appellant(s) / Petitioner(s)\nVersus\nThe Commissioner, HR&CE Department, Chennai & Joint Commissioner, Madurai\n... Respondent(s) / State\n\nSTATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:\nTamil Nadu Hindu Religious and Charitable Endowments Act 1959, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:\nHR&CE Act Section 78, HR&CE Act Section 79, Article 226\n\nKEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:\nTemple Lands, HR&CE, Encroachment, Public Trust, Parens Patriae\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTUAL MATRIX:\nEncroachers erected commercial shops on 12 acres of ancient temple property in Madurai without valid lease. HR&CE failed to enforce eviction under Section 78.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:\n1. Does the Court have duty under Parens Patriae jurisdiction to protect temple properties from unlawful alienation?\n\n3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:\nSections 78 and 79 HR&CE Act grant summary powers to evict encroachers of religious endowments.\n\n4. RATIO DECIDENDI:\nIdol is a perpetual minor; High Court exercising Parens Patriae jurisdiction is duty-bound to order eviction of encroachers from temple lands.\n\n5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; HR&CE Department directed to recover encroached temple lands within 90 days.\n\nDecreed and ordered accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]\n	3	t
