aterbody Protection Forum\n... Petitioner(s) / Appellant(s)\nVersus\nDistrict Collector, Chengalpattu & Member Secretary, CMDA\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nTamil Nadu Protection of Tanks and Eviction of Encroachment Act 2007, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nTN Act 8 of 2007 Section 7, Article 21, Article 48A, Article 51A(g)\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nWater Body Protection, Encroachment Removal, Public Trust Doctrine, Ecological Balance, Wetlands\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nLake catchment area measuring 45 acres was reclassified and encroached by commercial logistics park.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nCan government authorities regularize or reclassify water spread areas for industrial or commercial layouts?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nState holds all water bodies in public trust; no government authority has jurisdiction to reclassify water bodies or regularize catchment encroachments.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nWrit Petition Allowed; Encroachments in lake water-spread area ordered removed within 60 days.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Acting Chief Justice & Justice D. Bharatha Chakravarthy\nMadras High Court (Principal Seat, Chennai)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
