 / Appellant(s)\nVersus\nState represented by Inspector of Police, Alangulam Police Station, Tenkasi District\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nMines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Act 1957, Code of Criminal Procedure 1973\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nMMDR Act Section 21, CrPC Section 451, BNSS Section 497\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nIllegal Sand Mining, Vehicle Seizure, Interim Custody, Section 451 CrPC, District Mineral Foundation\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nVehicle seized for transporting river sand without valid e-transit pass. Magistrate dismissed interim custody petition.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nShould commercial vehicles seized in mineral offenses be kept idle in police stations causing natural decay?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nSeized commercial vehicles should not be allowed to rust at police stations; conditional interim custody must be granted under Sunderbhai Ambalal Desai.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nInterim Custody Granted with conditions; Tipper lorry released subject to deposit of Rs. 1 Lakh before mineral foundation.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice K.K. Ramakrishnan\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
