ured Quarry Worker)\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nEmployee's Compensation Act 1923\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nEmployee's Compensation Act Section 3, Employee's Compensation Act Section 4\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nWorkmen Compensation, Functional Disability, Total Incapacity, Employment Injury, Occupational Hazard\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nQuarry blaster suffered right arm amputation. Insurance company argued medical board assessed physical disability at only 65%.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nShould compensation be assessed on medical physical disability or functional loss of earning capacity?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nFunctional disability must be assessed based on the specific vocational work performed by the workman; 65% physical disability equals 100% functional loss.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCivil Miscellaneous Appeal Dismissed; 100% loss of earning capacity upheld for quarry blaster suffering limb amputation.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
