ent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nCode of Criminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nCrPC Section 125, BNSS Section 144, CrPC Section 397\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nMaintenance, Section 125 CrPC, Standard of Living, Income Tax Returns, Financial Capacity\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nHusband, earning Rs. 1.2 Lakhs as government school headmaster, neglected wife and daughter. Trial court granted meager Rs. 6,000.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nWhat is the quantum benchmark for maintenance under Section 125 CrPC / 144 BNSS relative to husband's net salary?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nWife and children are entitled to live with identical socioeconomic dignity and comfort enjoyed in the matrimonial household.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCriminal Revision Allowed; Maintenance enhanced from Rs. 6,000 to Rs. 22,000 per month reflecting husband's IT returns.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi\nMadras High Court (Madurai Bench)\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
