ion\n... Petitioner(s) / Appellant(s)\nVersus\nUnion of India, Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nDigital Personal Data Protection Act 2023, Consumer Protection Act 2019, Constitution of India\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nDPDP Act Section 6, Article 21, Consumer Protection Act Section 2(9)\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nDark Patterns, Digital Privacy, Informed Consent, Data Autonomy, K.S. Puttaswamy\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nChallenge to pre-checked cookie consents and deceptive subscription interfaces on government and commercial portals.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nDo dark patterns that nudge users into involuntarily relinquishing personal data breach the constitutional right to privacy?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nConsent procured through dark patterns or UI deception is null and void ab initio; true digital consent must be freely given, specific, and unambiguous.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCivil Appeal Allowed; Automated dark patterns and deceptive consent mechanisms declared violative of digital privacy.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice Sanjiv Khanna & Justice B.V. Nagarathna\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
