ustice Surya Kant & Justice K.V. Viswanathan\n\nPARTIES:\nPhoenix ARC Private Limited (Asset Reconstruction Company)\n... Petitioner(s) / Appellant(s)\nVersus\nKetan Patel & Anr. (Borrowers)\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nSecuritisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest Act 2002\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nSARFAESI Act Section 13(2), SARFAESI Act Section 13(4), SARFAESI Act Section 17\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nSARFAESI, Asset Reconstruction, Secured Creditor, DRT Jurisdiction, Non-Performing Asset\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nHigh Court entertained Article 226 writ petition and stayed SARFAESI auction of secured asset despite borrower bypassing DRT under Section 17.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nCan High Court exercise writ jurisdiction under Article 226 to stall auction proceedings under Section 13(4) of SARFAESI Act?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nHigh Courts should not entertain writ petitions challenging SARFAESI actions when effective statutory remedy exists before DRT under Section 17.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCivil Appeal Allowed; High Court order staying SARFAESI auction quashed; Section 17 DRT remedy is exclusive.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice Surya Kant & Justice K.V. Viswanathan\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
