pondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nConstitution of India, Special Marriage Act 1954\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nArticle 14, Article 15, Article 21, Article 44\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nGender Justice, Matrimonial Equality, Article 44, Succession Rights, Law Commission\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nPublic interest litigation seeking uniform matrimonial property rights and maintenance standards for women regardless of religious denomination.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nDoes disparity in maintenance and succession laws across personal codes violate equality under Articles 14 and 15?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nGender justice and equal matrimonial protections are fundamental constitutional imperatives that transcend statutory distinctions.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nWrit Petition Disposed; Law Commission requested to submit final report on inter-faith matrimonial equality within 6 months.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Constitution Bench (3 Judges)\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
