/ Appellant(s)\nVersus\nSanjay Nirupam (Accused on Bail)\n... Respondent(s)\n\nSTATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:\nCode of Criminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023\n\nSECTIONS & PROVISIONS:\nCrPC Section 437(5), CrPC Section 439(2), BNSS Section 483(3)\n\nKEY TOPICS & ISSUES:\nBail Cancellation, Supervening Circumstances, Tampering with Evidence, Personal Liberty, High Threshold\n\n================================================================================\n                                   JUDGMENT\n================================================================================\n\n1. FACTS OF THE CASE:\nState sought cancellation of bail granted to political activist on grounds that he addressed public rallies criticizing the investigating agency.\n\n2. ISSUES FRAMED:\nWhat constitute valid legal grounds for cancelling bail under Section 439(2) CrPC / Section 483(3) BNSS?\n\n3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:\nRejection of bail and cancellation of bail stand on entirely different legal footings; bail cannot be cancelled without cogent proof of witness tampering.\n\n4. FINAL ORDER:\nCriminal Appeal Dismissed; Bail cancellation refused; No evidence of witness tampering or misuse of liberty.\n\nOrdered and decreed accordingly.\n\nHon'ble Justice B.R. Gavai & Justice Sandeep Mehta\nSupreme Court of India\n[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]\n	3	t
