lic Prosecutor for the\nRespondent-State.\n2. By the present Petition iled under Article 227 of the\nConstitution of India, the Petitioner has sought the following\nsubstantive relief:\n“(a) hat this Hon’ble Court in exercise of its inherent\njurisdiction under Section 482 Code of Criminal\nProcedure, be pleased to quash and set aside Impugned\nJudgment and Order dated 11.01.22 of the Addl. Sessions\nJudge at Margao in Criminal Revision Application\nNo.33/20.”\nPage 1 of 2\n21st October 2026\n\n--- PAGE 2 ---\n903-WPCR-18-2023.DOC\n3. his matter was heard for some time on 19.10.2026. Mr\nToraskar, learned Advocate for the Petitioner sought an\naccommodation to take instructions from the Petitioner. As such,\nthis Petition was listed today.\n4. Today, Mr Toraskar, learned Advocate for the Petitioner on\ninstructions of the Petitioner, seeks leave to withdraw the present\nPetition with liberty to take recourse to the civil remedies as\navailable to the Petitioner in respect of the DC proceedings\nbearing No.88.\n5. Mr Karpe, learned Additional Public Prosecutor for the\nRespondent-State does not oppose the request made by Mr\nToraskar, learned Advocate for the Petitioner and submits that all\nthe civil remedies of the Petitioner can be left open.\n6. In view of the statement made by Mr Toraskar, learned\nAdvocate for the Petitioner, leave is granted to withdraw this\nPetition with liberty as prayed. If the Petitioner intends to ile\nany proceedings enforcing his civil rights, all contentions of the\nPetitioner are left open. If such proceedings are iled, the same be\nconsidered on its own merits and in accordance with law.\n7. Criminal Writ Petition is disposed of in the above terms.\nASHWIN D. BHOBE, J.\nPage 2 of 2\n21st October 2026	2	t
